# Installed by `npm install`.
node_modules/

# Build output — `npm run build` regenerates it.
dist/

# Android debug APK. The `android/` project itself IS committed (it holds the
# landscape lock in AndroidManifest.xml); only the build outputs and the
# machine-specific SDK path are not.
build/
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/

# Local dev server log.
.vite.log

# Local editor/agent settings, including machine-specific paths.
.claude/

# WAM — the art-model language the item models are authored in. It is its own
# git repository with its own history, so committing it here would store a
# submodule pointer and clone as an empty folder. The game does not need it to
# run: the compiled models it loads are in `public/models/wam/`, which ARE
# committed.
#
# Our own `.wam` sources are NOT in here — they are in `art/wam/`, tracked
# normally. They used to live inside this clone, which meant every model the
# project has ever authored was untracked by both repositories at once: this
# one ignores the folder, and the clone belongs to somebody else. The compiled
# output was safe and the source that made it was not. Nothing of ours goes
# back in here; see `art/wam/README.md`.
# Anchored, and it has to be. Bare `wam` matches a directory of that name at
# *any* depth, so it also swallowed `public/models/wam/` — the one thing this
# comment says is committed. The models already in there were force-added
# before anyone noticed; every new one was silently invisible to `git add`.
/wam/

# The Lynocs texture pack is not redistributed here — see CREDITS.md. The bake
# script reads it from a path outside this tree, and the baked atlases it
# produces (`public/tiles/`) are committed so the game runs without it.
